{
  "slug": "windows-11-battery-drains-fast",
  "title": "7 Ways to Fix a Fast-Draining Windows 11 Battery",
  "description": "Windows 11 battery drains fast? Find the apps that use the most power and stop them. Run 7 fixes, from battery saver to a battery report.",
  "category": "PC Troubleshooting",
  "tags": [
    "Windows",
    "PC Maintenance",
    "Troubleshooting",
    "Beginner Guide"
  ],
  "url": "https://www.techtips.fun/blog/windows-11-battery-drains-fast/",
  "theme": "github-dark",
  "durationInFrames": 930,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "title": "7 Ways to Fix a Fast-Draining Windows 11 Battery",
      "subtitle": "Windows 11 battery drains fast? Find the apps that use the most power and stop them.",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Before You Start",
      "body": "Connect the charger before you start the fixes. Make sure that the charger works. The battery icon must show a charge.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 1: Lower the Brightness and Turn On Battery Saver",
      "body": "The screen uses the most power on a laptop. Battery saver reduces the power use of every app. Open Settings. Select System > Power & battery.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 2: Find the Apps That Use the Most Power",
      "body": "Windows shows the power use for every app. One app can drain the battery by itself. Open Settings. Select System > Power & battery.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 3: Shorten the Screen and Sleep Times",
      "body": "Windows keeps the screen on for the time that you set. The screen uses power the whole time. Open Settings. Select System > Power & battery.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 4: Disable the Startup Apps",
      "body": "Startup apps start with Windows. These apps use the battery before you open them. Right-click the Start button. Select Task Manager.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 5: Turn Off the Radio Connections and Syncing",
      "body": "The Wi-Fi and the Bluetooth connections use power in the background. Sync services such as OneDrive also use the battery.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "heading": "Read the full article",
      "body": "New posts every week on the blog.",
      "url": "techtips.fun",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    }
  ],
